From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 09:59:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 78/78] web-app: SlothfulChat welcome message in the device
 chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The device chat opened with Delta Chat's welcome message and nothing
about what this fork actually is, so nothing told a first-time user that
their account lives in the browser — or that they should back it up.

Add a second device message after core's own: fork of Delta Chat (not
directly affiliated), runs fully in the browser via WebAssembly,
installable to the home screen, back your data up because clearing site
data wipes it and the backup is unencrypted, expect prototype churn, and
it can be self-hosted or forked.

It is added from selectAccount() rather than updateDeviceChat(): that one
is deliberately skipped for freshly created accounts and runs before
configure(), which is when core adds its welcome message — ours has to
land after it. selectAccount() is also reached on the unconfigured ->
configured transition, so a brand-new account gets it as soon as
onboarding finishes; the device-message label makes every later call a
no-op, so re-running it on each account switch costs nothing.

The paragraph pointing at the "Sloth (Slothful.chat Developer)" entry in
New Chat is dropped when SLOTHFUL_HIDE_PUBLIC_SUGGESTIONS hid that entry
for the instance, so a self-hosted build never sends its users looking
for something it doesn't ship.
